What's new (Mon Oct 26 16:40:00 UTC 2026):

*) Downloads are now incremental without "-nc": every transfer first compares
   the local size with the server's Content-Length (.zip archives are also
   tested with "unzip -t"), so a complete file is not downloaded again while a
   truncated or damaged one is repaired instead of staying in the mirror
   forever. "force" re-checks a release and fetches only what is broken.
*) Transfers go to <file>.part and are renamed only after the size/CRC check,
   so an interrupted run cannot leave a half-written .npk/.zip under its real
   name; no .part files are left behind.
*) Version marker answers are validated against "<version> <timestamp>" before
   being used (an HTML error page from a proxy can no longer create a garbage
   directory or overwrite a working marker); a leftover marker .new file is
   removed at the start of every check, so one failed check no longer blocks
   the ROS 7 synchronization permanently.
*) Winbox: curl is called with --fail, the body is checked for an HTML error
   page and .zip files for archive integrity; previously a 404 page was stored
   as winbox.zip and then kept forever by the "file already exists" check.
*) New releases now reach the devices: promoting a version clears
   ros6.version.cache / ros7.version.cache, cached answers are re-validated
   against upstream once they are older than "cache_revalidate" (6 hours by
   default) instead of being final forever, and writeCacheIfChanged refreshes
   the timestamp also when the answer did not change.
*) Degradation order fixed: an expired cache entry is served as X-Cache: STALE
   before falling back to local markers and the configured fallbacks.
*) ros-warmup.php re-validates aged entries instead of skipping anything that
   is cached and reports changed answers as CHANGE (report: OK/CHANGE/SKIP/FAIL);
   the Dockerfile build patch now rewrites the WARMUP_URL line.
*) wget gets --timeout/--read-timeout/--tries, sync_mikrotik_repo.sh and
   download_ros.sh share a lock file, the mirror directory is created before
   the write permission test, and the real exit code is propagated (no more
   unconditional "exit 0", config.sh errors no longer kill the caller).
*) Proxy caches and transfer artifacts (*.cache, *.part, *.new, *.tmp under
   /routeros) are denied in the nginx and Apache configurations.
*) docs/README.ru.md, docs/README.md and docker/README.md updated accordingly.

